{"step_index":1282,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-22T12:04:36Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-22T17:34:36+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-09-22T17:34:36+05:30\nFile Path: `file:///c:/Users/k4ran/OneDrive/Desktop/smartAGENT/README.md`\nTotal Lines: 111\nTotal Bytes: 4349\nShowing lines 1 to 111\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: # 🛡️ SmartAGENT & Fluxnat Coder 3B\n2: \n3: An AI-powered cybersecurity vulnerability scanner and specialized 3B Small Language Model (SLM) fine-tuning suite for autonomous source code security audits.\n4: \n5: ---\n6: \n7: ## 🌟 Highlights\n8: \n9: - **🧠 Fluxnat Coder 3B:** Specialized cybersecurity Small Language Model (SLM) trained and developed by Fluxnat. Refusal-free for security assessment and vulnerability analysis.\n10: - **⚡ 3-Layer Hybrid Architecture:** Deterministic SAST Scanners (Secrets, Patterns, Dependencies, Configs) + AI Chain-of-Thought Judge + Security Scoring.\n11: - **☁️ 1-Click Google Colab Training:** Includes `Fluxnat_Coder_3B_Training.ipynb` configured with **Unsloth (2x faster, 70% less VRAM)** to train on a **free Tesla T4 GPU (16GB VRAM)**.\n12: - **📊 Precision Security Grading:** Computes vulnerability deduction index (0–100) and letter grades (A+ to F).\n13: - **🔧 Direct CLI Integration:** Scan local projects or directories with `smartagent scan .`.\n14: \n15: ---\n16: \n17: ## 📁 Repository Structure\n18: \n19: ```\n20: smartAGENT/\n21: ├── Fluxnat_Coder_3B_Training.ipynb   # 1-Click Google Colab Training Notebook\n22: ├── pyproject.toml                     # Dependencies & package metadata\n23: ├── prepare_datasets.py                # Dataset download, cleaning & formatting\n24: ├── train.py                           # Unsloth / PEFT QLoRA training engine\n25: ├── rebrand.py                         # Deep config & metadata rebranding engine\n26: ├── merge_and_export.py                # 16-bit stan\n<truncated 1235 bytes>\nhain-of-thought prompt templates\n45: │   └── reporting/\n46: │       ├── report.py                  # Rich terminal UI & exports\n47: │       └── scorer.py                  # Security score (A+ to F)\n48: └── tests/\n49:     └── test_scanners.py               # Unit tests\n50: ```\n51: \n52: ---\n53: \n54: ## 🚀 Quick Start: Training Fluxnat Coder 3B\n55: \n56: ### Option A: Google Colab (Recommended - Free GPU)\n57: 1. Open [Google Colab](https://colab.research.google.com).\n58: 2. Upload `Fluxnat_Coder_3B_Training.ipynb`.\n59: 3. Set runtime to **GPU (T4)**.\n60: 4. Run all cells — it will automatically train, merge, rebrand, and push `fluxnat/Fluxnat-Coder-3B` to Hugging Face!\n61: \n62: ### Option B: Local Training (RTX 3060/4060 or higher)\n63: ```bash\n64: # 1. Install dependencies\n65: pip install -e .\n66: \n67: # 2. Prepare datasets\n68: python prepare_datasets.py\n69: \n70: # 3. Launch training\n71: python train.py\n72: \n73: # 4. Merge adapters and export standalone model\n74: python merge_and_export.py\n75: \n76: # 5. Benchmark the model\n77: python evaluate.py\n78: ```\n79: \n80: ---\n81: \n82: ## 🔍 Using SmartAGENT Scanner\n83: \n84: ### 1. Basic Scan (Fast Static Pass)\n85: ```bash\n86: smartagent scan /path/to/your/project\n87: ```\n88: \n89: ### 2. AI-Verified Scan (with Fluxnat Coder 3B)\n90: Uses the AI model to eliminate false positives and generate exact fix snippets:\n91: ```bash\n92: smartagent scan /path/to/your/project --ai\n93: ```\n94: \n95: ### 3. Export Reports (JSON & Markdown)\n96: ```bash\n97: smartagent scan /path/to/your/project --json report.json --md report.md\n98: ```\n99: \n100: ### 4. Check Environment Status\n101: ```bash\n102: smartagent info\n103: ```\n104: \n105: ---\n106: \n107: ## ⚖️ License & Ethical Use\n108: \n109: SmartAGENT and Fluxnat Coder 3B are licensed under the **Apache-2.0 License**.\n110: Designed for defensive security auditing, vulnerability triage, and authorized penetration testing.\n111: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
